2. KERS & INERTIA MANAGEMENT (THE 0 RPM STRATEGY)\
The system intentionally decelerates the lifted axle to 
\f2\b 0 RPM
\f1\b0  to maximize efficiency and stability.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f2\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Energy Harvesting:
\f1\b0  When an axle is lifted at high velocity (e.g., 90 km/h), the hub-integrated electric motor switches to 
\f2\b Generator Mode
\f1\b0  to brake the rotating mass.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Storage:
\f1\b0  The captured kinetic energy is converted into electricity and stored in supercapacitors or the vehicle's battery bank.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Reuse:
\f1\b0  This energy is later deployed to power the 
\f2\b e-Sync phase
\f1\b0  (accelerating the next axle in the air), making the transition energy-neutral.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Stability:
\f1\b0  Reducing the lifted tires to 0 RPM eliminates 
\f2\b gyroscopic precession forces
\f1\b0 , significantly improving vehicle handling in corners.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
